Quoting  Oliver Scholz  <alkibiades@gmx.de>:
>I am playing a Level 1 Samurai, I am currently at dlvl 1 with a large
>dog as a pet. In "Maniac's Ascension Guide (3.4.2)", which I found on
>the internet, I read about playing with a pacifist conduct in the
>early levels. The idea is to make it to the Minetown while still at
>level 1 and in order to buy cheap protection from the priest there.

Yes, that's one of the stupidest pieces of advice in the MAG. The
protection racket is, at best, suitable for expert players with characters
particularly suited to it.

>I know I can gain that from eating a floating eye; and I know how to
>kill a floating eye, in fact I already have a blind fold. But how do I
>kill one without breaking the pacifist conduct? (I wouldn't mind
>breaking it, actually, but in my experience doing so would level my
>clvl 1 character up immediately.)

A floating eye is normally worth 17 experience points; hence you can do so
but have leeway only to kill 2 1-XP monsters.

If you are going to do the racket you should know the normal XP value of
all monsters you are likely to meet.
